# Tablevera mobile (`apps/mobile`)

Expo SDK 57 + React Native + Expo Router + Apollo Client + Zustand (MMKV) +
react-native-unistyles 3. Custom components only — no third-party UI libraries.
Icons are Lucide paths rendered with `react-native-svg`.

This is the **diner** client for Tablevera (OpenTable/Resy-style reservations).
It lives in the `uzeats-reservations` pnpm + Turborepo monorepo as
`@reservations/mobile`. GraphQL is served by `apps/api` at `/graphql`.

## API

- Default: `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL` or `http://localhost:4000/graphql`
- Preview/production EAS builds use `https://api.tablevera.online/graphql`
- Auth tokens: `expo-secure-store` (`accessToken`, `refreshToken`)
- Prefer existing ops in `src/graphql/operations.ts`; align with
  `apps/api/src/graphql/typeDefs.ts`
- Deposit PaymentSheet: set `EXPO_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` (local `.env` or
  EAS secret). API must have `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` or it auto-authorizes stubs and
  never returns a presentable `clientSecret`.

## Theme

- Root `unistyles.ts` — Forest & Gold light theme only
- Typography: **DM Sans only** (see components rule)
- Always use `theme.colors.*`, `theme.space(n)`, `theme.radius.*`
- Never hardcode hex colors or raw pixel spacing in features/components

## Run (dev client required — not Expo Go)

```bash
# from repo root
pnpm install
pnpm --filter @reservations/mobile start

# first-time native binary (your EAS account):
cd apps/mobile && eas build --profile development --platform ios
# then install the build and start with --dev-client
```

Local API: start `apps/api`, set `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL` to your machine IP on device.
